ate start=\"2026-11-17\" /> after the user rejected the proposal with the reason ‚ÄúFalta transfer 1 C 126cm‚Äù.\n\nReference: <mention url=\"https://app.notion.com/p/074b6705ae1f8257a53701d87a64eb32\">428 ‚Äî AVENTAL grande com bolso - 2F</mention>.\n\n| Location | Original option | Confirmed New option |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Bolso | Transfer - At√© 126 cm2 - 2 Cores (aprox. 11,2x11,2cm - MOCHILA) | <b>Transfer - At√© 126 cm2 - 1 Cor (aprox. 11,2x11,2cm - MOCHILA)</b> |\n\n- Retain Transfer for this confirmed pocket option; change the colour selection from 2 colours to 1 colour while preserving the exact 126 cm¬≤ specification.\n- Keep DTF A6 as the existing separate proposal; it does not replace the confirmed one-colour Transfer option. The technical mapping of ‚Äúcolours‚Äù still needs confirmation.\n- This confirms the PP428 pocket mapping. Do not infer new mappings for other profiles without checking their source, category rules and user decisions.\n- The current IMP ‚Üí New list omits generic Transfer entries, while the existing database option catalogue includes Transfer up to 126 cm¬≤, 1 colour. Record this discrepancy; it is not a reason to drop the user-confirmed option. This rule update does not itself edit the IMP list.\n- Add the confirmed option to both the per-location New table and the global <code>Op√ß√µes de personaliza√ß√£o</code> property. Include Transfer in <code>T√©cnicas</code>.\n- Preserve the user's rejection and explanation. Recording a correction does not mark the PP approved.\n\n## Preservation and consistency when applying these rules\n\nPreserve the PP code, product identity, images, notes, the Original configuration and original Excel evidence. Prepare and verify the New configuration per location, using exact existing technical option names. Keep different locations separate; do not replace their mappings with a single flat list.\n\n<b>Updated user instruction:</b> when a reviewed New configuration is applied, the page properties must agree with it: <code>Faces</code> and <code>N√∫mero de locais poss√≠veis</code> reflect its locations; <code>T√©cnicas</code> and <code>Op√ß√µes de personaliza√ß√£o</code> reflect the combined options actually assigned in New. Preserve the original values in Old/source history and record the change. This supersedes the earlier instruction to leave the global options property unchanged, which remains visible only in the historical PP49 reference below.\n\nUnknown associations remain unresolved rather than being invented. Keep the PP <code>A rever</code> while approval is outstanding, and preserve the Yes/No decision and rejection reason for later review.\n\n<toggle heading=\"h2\">\nEarlier PP49 example and method (historical reference)\n\nThe text below is preserved for traceability. The category rules above extend the earlier PP49-only evidence. Technique substitutions in this earlier example must not override the unresolved mapping limits above.\n\n# PP transformation logic ‚Äî validated example: PP 49\n\n<callout icon=\"‚úÖ\" color=\"green_bg\">\n<b>Validated basis:</b> PP 49 (adult short-sleeved T-shirts and polos). Keep the existing printing locations, but standardize the selected printing options using the <code>IMP ‚Üí New</code> list. This is a reusable method, not an automatic rule for every PP. Changes to other profiles require category-specific validation and authorization.\n</callout>\n\nReference: <mention url=\"https://app.notion.com/p/cbbb6705ae1f822790c601b6be542afc\">49 ‚Äî T√äXTIL ADULTO Manga Curta - T-shirts/Polos</mention>.\n\n## 1. Core transformation rules\n\n| Element | Rule |\n| --- | --- |\n| C√≥digo PP | Never change |\n| Product name and classification | Preserve |\n| Faces / Locais | Preserve all existing locations |\n| Printing techniques | Use the options listed in <code>IMP ‚Üí New</code> |\n| Printing sizes | Use the approved reference size for each location |\n| Number of colors | Follow the exact option in IMP |\n| <code>Op√ß√µes de personaliza√ß√£o</code> property | <b>Keep completely unchanged</b> |\n| Original Excel data | Preserve |\n| Images and notes | Preserve |\n\n## 2. Location determines the printing size\n\nFor PP 49, the validated mappings are:\n\n| Printing location | Reference size | Matching options in IMP ‚Üí New |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Peito Esquerdo / Peito Direito | <b>A7</b> | Estamparia ‚Äî 1 Cor (A7); DTF ‚Äî A7; Bordado ‚Äî 60 cm¬≤ |\n| Manga Esquerda / Manga Direita | <b>A7</b> | Estamparia ‚Äî 1 Cor (A7); DTF ‚Äî A7; Bordado ‚Äî 60 cm¬≤ |\n| Frente / Costas | <b>A4</b> | Estamparia ‚Äî 1 Cor (A4); DTF ‚Äî A4; Bordado ‚Äî 600 cm¬≤ |\n\n### Exact existing IMP option names used in PP 49\n\n<b>A7 ‚Äî Peito / Mangas</b>\n\n- Estamparia - At√© A7 - 1 Cor (BOLSO \\| MANGA)\n- DTF - At√© A7 (7,4x10,5cm - BOLSO \\| MANGA \\| ESTOJOS)\n- Bordado - At√© 60 cm2 - At√© 7,7x7,7 aprox. - BOLSO \\| BONE \\| MANGA - A7\n\n<b>A4 ‚Äî Frente / Costas</b>\n\n- Estamparia - At√© A4 - 1 Cor\n- DTF - At√© A4 (21x29,7cm)\n- Bordado - At√© 600 cm2 - At√© 24,5x24,5cm aprox. - A4\n\nThe A7/A4 mapping is validated for the PP 49 example only. Other product categories may require different sizes.\n\n## 3. How to transform individual techniques\n\n| Technique | Transformation logic illustrated by PP 49 |\n| --- | --- |\n| Estamparia<br />Transfer | Replace the 4-colour selection with the corresponding 1-colour option from IMP ‚Üí New<br /><br />transfer 2 cores - para 1 cor |\n| DTF<br />Flex | Keep DTF, Flex selecting only the approved reference size for the location |\n| Bordado | Select the IMP embroidery option corresponding to that location's reference size |\n| Other techniques | Do not add or replace techniques without confirming the relevant product rules |\n\nFor example, the original Frente/Costas configuration included A3 options. The validated PP 49 example selects A4 instead. <b>A3 is excluded only from the proposed face-by-face selection, not deleted from the original technical data.</b>\n\n## 4. Workflow for future PP updates\n\n1. <b>Identify the PP.</b> Read its category, product characteristics, materials, and existing locations.\n2. <b>Read the current configuration.</b> Extract every face/local and its associated printing options.\n3. <b>Determine the correct reference size.</b> Apply the relevant PDF/email rule. For PP 49, use A7 for chest/sleeves and A4 for front/back.\n4. <b>Match options against IMP ‚Üí New.</b> Use the exact existing names, dimensions, and technical descriptions. Do not invent new options.\n5. <b>Generate the new face-by-face configuration.</b> Retain compatible techniques, use the approved sizes, and exclude options outside the defined selection.\n6. <b>Preserve original technical information.</b> Do not change the <code>Op√ß√µes de personaliza√ß√£o</code> property, original Excel data, images, or historical notes.\n7. <b>Verify the result.</b> Compare Old versus New, flag uncertain compatibility, and obtain authorization before modifying a PP.\n\n## 5. What must not be generalized\n\nThe PP 49 example confirms a method, not a universal rule for all 814 PPs.\n\n- Do not assume that every textile item supports embroidery.\n- Do not replace every Estamparia option with 1 Cor without checking the relevant approved category rules.\n- Do not apply A7/A4 indiscriminately to bottles, notebooks, bags, or other product categories.\n- Do not assume that the largest printing size is always the correct reference size.\n- Respect special cases, including sublimation-only products and <b>PP 601 ‚Äî n√£o mexer</b>.\n\n## 6. Reusable decision sequence\n\n<callout icon=\"üìê\" color=\"gray_bg\">\n<b>For each existing printing location:</b>\n\nProduct category + Material + Location\n\n‚Üí Approved printing size\n\n‚Üí Matching options from IMP ‚Üí New\n\n‚Üí New face-by-face configuration\n</callout>\n\n<b>Conclusion:</b> The PP 49 Old ‚Üí New comparison is the validated transformation example for adult short-sleeved T-shirts an